<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $195.6 mln Sept 5.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $195.6 mln Sept 5.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $195.6 million deficit on September 5 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON SEPTEMBER 5</p>
<p>Exports: $206 million</p>
<p>Imports: $182.8 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $103.5 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $322.3 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $195.6 million</p>
<p>SEPTEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $909.5 million</p>
<p>Imports: $558.6 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $423 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $719.6 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $54.3 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
